Status: blame counts are done, and I'm writing up the result now.

## Window: 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-12 (14 days up to the latest commit)

I used explicit dates, not `--since=14d`. The latest commit is 2026-04-12 and today is 2026-10-22, so a relative window would be empty. I did not launch the contributor-analyzer agent because the window has only 4 commits.

| Person | Commits in window | Lines still in code |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 2 (`02afce3`, `b2005d9`) | 48 (36 + 12) |
| Vansh Sharma | 1 (`5317ebe`) | 1 |

- **Troy Goode, `02afce3`** (test: vary header coverage): +36 lines, all 36 still present.
- **Troy Goode, `b2005d9`** (lib: annotate handlers): 12 lines changed. All 12 survive when `git blame -w` ignores whitespace. Under strict blame only 1 survives, because the later reformat commit took over the other 11. I counted 12 because that commit only re-indented and re-quoted them. If you want strict blame, Troy's total is 37.
- **Vansh Sharma, `5317ebe`** (docs: README `app.del()` → `app.delete()`): 1 line changed, and it is still there.

## Excluded
- **Fiona Formatter**, `62628c0` (style: reformat JS, +1016/−1016): formatting-only commit.
- **dependabot[bot]**: no commits in this window. Its latest commits are from 2026-03-02.

## Counted once
Each person appears under one name and one email. There is no `.mailmap`, and I found no duplicate identities.
